  SPACE_AUTO_LATEST_OLV_TT: "Fly only the newest launch vehicle you have researched.\n\nOff, automation flies the §Yoldest rocket in stock that can still lift the manifest§! and keeps the newest generation on order, so stages left over from an earlier generation get spent instead of sitting in the hangar. An older rocket lifts less, so those flights carry a smaller manifest.\n\nOn, older stages are ignored entirely. Every flight carries the full manifest, but the program waits on new rockets rather than launching what it already has."
  SPACE_AUTO_LATEST_OLV_TT_DELAYED: "Turn this on when your leftover stages are too small to be worth a launch slot, and off when you would rather clear the hangar than wait.\n\n§RSPYSAT payloads weigh exactly what the matching rocket can lift§!. On a spy-satellite plan an older stage can never carry the newest generation, so this switch changes nothing there."
